@doc hr_memorandum
@meta title: HR memorandum on a workplace complaint
@meta subject: Complaint under the respectful workplace policy
@meta traps: an official appearing as a complainant in their own grievance is R1, not K2
@cast hr=official grievant=official respondent=official adm=official requester=requester
@block letterhead
{hr.organisation}
Human Resources Division - IN CONFIDENCE

@block body
MEMORANDUM

To: {adm.full_name}, {adm.title}
From: {hr.full_name}, {hr.title}
Date: 11 May
Subject: Complaint under the Respectful Workplace Policy - file {hr.file_number!K6}

@block body
This memorandum sets out the findings of the review I was asked to conduct.

The complaint was made by {grievant.full_name!R1}, who is employed in this Department as
{grievant.title}. In the complaint {grievant.given_name!R1} describes a pattern of
conduct over eleven months and states that the conduct has affected their health. A
medical certificate was provided in support and is held separately; it records a period
of leave from 3 February and gives a personal contact number of
{grievant.personal_phone!R1}. {grievant.given_name!R1} asked that their home address,
{grievant.home_address!R1}, not be shared with the respondent.

The complaint names {respondent.full_name}, {respondent.title}, as the respondent. The
conduct described concerns the allocation of work and the conduct of team meetings, all
of it within the respondent's duties as {respondent.title}. {respondent.given_name}
responded in writing on 24 April and was interviewed on 2 May.

@block body
Two further employees were interviewed. Both spoke about the operation of the unit rather
than about either party personally, and both asked that their accounts be attributed to
their positions rather than to their names.

A member of the public, {requester.full_name}, who had a service complaint outstanding
during the same period, is named in the complaint file at Tab 6 because a meeting about
that complaint is one of the incidents described. Nothing in this review concerns
{requester.given_name}'s own matter and no finding is made about it.

@block body
Findings: the allegation of an unreasonable allocation of work is not substantiated. The
allegation concerning the conduct of meetings is partly substantiated. I recommend
mediation and a review of the unit's meeting practice.

@block signature
{hr.full_name}
{hr.title}
{hr.work_email}
